  "methodology": "Isolated Xvfb display and private D-Bus session with a dedicated AT-SPI accessibility bus. The real MainWindow ran on the xcb platform with Qt's AT-SPI adaptor enabled. Orca 46.1 attached to the bus as a live screen reader with debug logging. A pyatspi client (the same client library Orca uses) verified every D4 inventory control publishes its accessible name over the bus and recorded focus events while the application walked keyboard focus through its focusable controls; Orca's debug log had to contain a SPEECH OUTPUT utterance naming every focused control. Transport buttons are deliberately NoFocus (their commands are global shortcuts), so they are verified via the bus tree walk rather than the focus walk.",
